    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0949" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg939"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-02-14T11:00:00+07:00">February 14,
                            1946—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>294. From Adler to the Secretary of the Treasury. After a conversation with
                    General Marshall, T. V. Soong agreed (re your telegram 85 of January 14) to
                    accept the offset principle with respect to Chinese requisitions of surplus
                    property. [Adler.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
